           \n\n                    \n                        \n                        <p><i>Nature</i>’s report on artificial-intelligence tools being used to detect long-standing errors in scientific papers illustrates that retrospective scrutiny is possible (see <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-02235-8\" data-track=\"click\" data-label=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-02235-8\" data-track-category=\"body text link\"><i>Nature</i> <b>656</b>, 278–279; 2026</a>). Such checks would be more robust if the tools had access to the original files.</p>\n                        \n                    \n                        <p><em>Nature</em> <strong>658</strong>, 834 (2026)</p>\n                        <p><em>doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-03244-3</em></p>\n\n                    \n                    <div id=\"competing-interests\" data-toggle=\"anchor-links-section\" data-label=\"Competing Interests\">\n                            <h2>Competing Interests</h2>\n                            <p>The authors declare no competing interests.</p>\n                        </div>\n\n                    \n                        \n    <h2>Related Articles</h2>\n    <ul data-track-context=\"related articles on news reading companion\">\n        \n            <li>\n                <p>\n                    <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02235-8\" data-track=\"select_article\" data-track-action=\"view related article\" data-track-index=\"1\">\n                        \n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"//media.nature.com/lw100/magazine-assets/d41586-026-03244-3/d41586-026-03244-3_53840324.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n                        \n                        AI agents are checking the scientific literature — and spotting decades-old errors\n                    </a>\n                </p>\n            </li>\n        \n            <li>\n                <p>\n                    <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586